{"fingerprint":"19cbdea3ffe3784e15ef53ac62aa2b0168ea6f41d892d54a8ce6877332154150","path":"src/review_gauntlet/git_worktree.py","rule_id":"cli-contract","content":"`_commit_session_changes` passes user-controlled `commit_paths` directly to `git add --`. If a caller passes paths containing `..` segments, files outside the worktree could be staged. The `merge_session_worktree` function validates `worktree_path` against path traversal but does not validate individual `commit_paths`. Consider normalising each path and verifying it stays within the worktree root.","suggestion_code":"def _commit_session_changes(
